===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To place inside a bucket.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To draw or lift in, or as if in, buckets.
#: {{ux|en|to '''bucket''' water}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|informal}} To [[rain]] heavily.
#: {{ux|en|It’s really '''bucketing''' down out there.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|informal}} To [[travel]] very [[quick]]ly.
#: {{ux|en|The boat is '''bucketing''' along.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[ride]] (a [[horse]]) hard or mercilessly.
# {{lb|en|transitive|AU|slang}} To [[criticize]] [[vehemently]]; to [[denigrate]].
# {{lb|en|computing|transitive}} To [[categorize]] (data) by splitting it into buckets, or groups of related items.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2002|author=Nicolò Cesa-Bianchi; Masayuki Numao; Rüdiger Reischuk|title=Algorithmic Learning Theory: 13th International Conference|page=352
|passage=These candidates are then '''bucketed''' into a discretized version of the space of all possible lines.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=Hari Mohan Pandey|title=Design Analysis and Algorithm|page=136|passage=Thus, sorting each bucket takes O(1) times. The total effort of '''bucketing''', sorting buckets, and concotenating{{SIC}} the sorted buckets together is O(''n'').}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|UK|US|rowing}} To make, or cause to make (the [[recovery]]), with a certain hurried or unskillful forward swing of the body.

